==English==

===Etymology===
Short for {{m|en|shove it up your ass}}.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{lb|en|vulgar}} {{non-gloss definition|Expression to show discontent with the other party, or to show contempt.}}
#: ''You dare come here dressed so horribly? Well, '''up yours!'''''
# {{lb|en|dismissive|vulgar}} [[go away|Go away]]! [[go to hell|Go to hell]]!
#: '''''Up yours!'''—I’m not giving you any!''
#: ''You’ve done enough to ruin our outing, so '''up yours!'''''

